# Mercury Edit 2 — findings by MiMo 2.6 Flash (self-excluded: no verified public benchmarks)

- Source: Inception (`inception/mercury-edit-2`)
- Date: 2026-11-12 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Mercury Edit 2
- **Short description:** Inception Labs' proprietary diffusion LLM (dLLM) for latency-sensitive code editing: fill-in-the-middle autocomplete plus next-edit prediction from recent edits and codebase context; KTO-aligned on human accept/reject feedback. Not a variant of a chat Mercury — a purpose-built edit-prediction endpoint (successor to Inception's previous next-edit model).
- **Provider / access:** Inception API — `POST https://api.inceptionlabs.ai/v1/fim/completions` (autocomplete) and `POST .../v1/edit/completions` (next-edit), non-OpenAI chat surface (no `v1/chat/completions`); integrated in Zed (edit prediction) and ProxyAI; provider catalog entry `inception/mercury-edit-2` active.
- **Release / knowledge:** vendor launch post "Introducing Mercury Edit 2" dated 2026-10-29 (provider catalog lists `released` 2026-03-30 — discrepancy noted, neither source resolves it); knowledge cutoff not published.
- **IDs:** `inception/mercury-edit-2` (API model `mercury-edit-2`); no OpenCode Zen Free ID exists (not in the provider catalog as a free/Zen entry as of 2026-11-12).
- **Context window:** 32,000 tokens for both FIM and NextEdit endpoints; max output 8,192 tokens (Inception docs, verified 2026-11-12). A third-party listing showing 128K conflicts with the vendor docs; vendor docs taken as authoritative.
- **Modalities:** text in; text out; non-reasoning (BenchLM); no chat, no tool calling, no structured outputs — FIM and edit-diff completion only.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-12):** $0.25 / 1M input, $0.75 / 1M output, $0.025 / 1M cached input (vendor docs, launch post, and provider catalog all agree); 10M free tokens on new Inception accounts; vendor blog also advertises a one-month Zed promo (promotional key on the launch post — not reproduced here).
- **Architecture:** proprietary diffusion language model (Mercury dLLM family); trained on curated multi-language edit datasets and aligned with Kahneman-Tversky Optimization (KTO) on recorded accept/reject preference data; parameter count not disclosed.

